-- title:
--   Right 𝒪-ideals represented by ideles supported at one split place
-- statement:
--   Let $c,d\in\mathbb Q$, let $q$ be a prime, and assume `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt c d q`, i.e. $c<0$, $d<0$ and, for every height-one prime $w$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$, the algebra $H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w$ (with $H=\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,c,d]$) has all nonzero elements invertible exactly when $q\in w$. Let $O\subseteq H$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule which is a maximal order: it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans $H$ over $\mathbb Q$, is finitely generated, and every order containing it equals it. Let $r$ be a prime with $r\neq q$ and $v$ a height-one prime with $r\in v$. Let $I\subseteq O$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule with $zo\in I$ for $z\in I$, $o\in O$, and $nO\subseteq I$ for some nonzero integer $n$. Then there exist $\beta\in H^\times$ and a unit $g$ of $H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ such that: the component of $g$ at every $w\neq v$ is $1$; for every ring isomorphism $\varphi:H\otimes\mathbb Q_v\cong M_2(\mathbb Q_v)$ with $\varphi(1\otimes t)=t\cdot 1$ and such that the additive group generated by the $z\otimes t$ with $z\in O$, $t\in\mathcal O_v$ is exactly $\varphi^{-1}(M_2(\mathcal O_v))$, both $\det\varphi(g_v)$ and $\det\varphi((g^{-1})_v)$ lie in $\mathcal O_v$; and, for $z\in H$, $z\in I$ iff $\beta^{-1}z$ lies in the preimage in $H$ of $g\cdot\widehat O$, where $\widehat O$ is the additive group generated by the $z\otimes a$ with $z\in O$ and $a$ an integral finite adele.
--
--   This is the statement that every right ideal of a maximal order in a definite rational quaternion algebra ramified exactly at $q$ admits, up to a global scalar $\beta$, an idelic generator concentrated at a prescribed split place $v$, with reduced norm a $v$-adic unit there; it combines local principality of right ideals with strong approximation for the norm-one group away from $v$. It is used to produce the matrix description of such ideals in [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsMaximalOrder.exists_matrix_forall_mulVec_mem_iff_of_le`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsMaximalOrder.exists_matrix_forall_mulVec_mem_iff_of_le).
